    [BugFix][KVPP] Complete Mooncake layerwise load synchronization (#19484)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    Complete KVPP + Mooncake block-key layerwise pooling on current main
    (rebased onto `3b845c4fe`). Refs #18448 and #18647.
    
    Main already has #18647's model-layer prefetch window and compact
    owner-relative Mooncake indices. Those fixes do not order external loads
    against KVPP broadcasts: the prefetch executor can broadcast a layer
    before its owner reloads it, while attention clears the completion event
    before the executor can observe it.
    
    Adapt the synchronization and object-isolation work from #18448:
    - Defer the first layerwise broadcast until attention prepares the
    connector load, and wait for owner-layer load completion before
    broadcasting. Keep the direct attention load/broadcast calls and the
    background non-consuming load-ready observer.
    - Retain load completion until the next metadata bind, and propagate
    receive-thread failures/aborts.
    - Finish Mooncake request loading even when the final physical layer has
    no owner-local tasks. Keep main's transfer-group/index routing
    unchanged.
    - Separate Mooncake KVPP objects from replicated-layout objects,
    including PP and multiple cache groups.
    - Adjust the PROLOG_V3 load ordering and avoid duplicate connector
    load-entry calls for mixed batches.
    - Detect AscendStore children in MultiConnector and forward the
    completion observer without advancing child attention cursors.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    No. This fixes synchronization bugs in the existing Mooncake layerwise +
    KVPP functionality; no new user-facing features, APIs, or configuration
    options are introduced.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    - **181 tests + 156 subtests passed** in a local CPU
    dependency-isolation harness, covering load/broadcast ordering,
    completion-event reset, failure propagation, request finalization,
    namespace isolation, and connector detection. This is not a native
    vLLM/NPU test run.
    - Source-method isolation checks covered MultiConnector forwarding and
    PROLOG_V3 load/broadcast ordering. Ruff, Markdownlint, Python
    compilation, and `git diff --check` passed. The full formatting command
    was blocked by local npm dependency installation.
    - Automated NPU E2E coverage was added in
    `tests/e2e/cases/features/kv_pool/test_kvpp_mooncake_layerwise.py`;
    execution of that suite remains pending.
    
    Performance measurements:
    
    | Devices | Model | Input | Output | Prefix hit rate | Deployment |
    Concurrency | Requests | TTFT (ms) | KVPP | Layerwise |
    | ------- | ----- | ----- | ------ | --------------- | ---------- |
    ----------- | -------- | --------- | ---- | --------- |
    | 8 | GLM-5.2-W4A8C8 | 128K | 1 | 90% | P/D mixed, TP8 | 32 | 128 |
    123.6 | Yes | No |
    | 8 | GLM-5.2-W4A8C8 | 128K | 1 | 90% | P/D mixed, TP8 | 32 | 128 |
    119.9 | No | Yes |
    | 8 | GLM-5.2-W4A8C8 | 128K | 1 | 90% | P/D mixed, TP8 | 32 | 128 |
    126.2 | Yes | Yes |
    
